From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] client: Leave with _exit() on a fatal connection error

0002 ends a client with exit(1) when the compositor goes away. exit() runs the
atexit handlers on whichever thread noticed, with the others still running. In
browser_shell the GPU thread then aborted in libhybris, or the Adreno driver's
destructors crashed in the allocator: a core dump for a compositor restart.

_exit() keeps what 0002 is for, and ends the process at once. Nothing a client
registered with atexit() runs, which is no loss here: the connection is gone,
and the handlers were not safe to run in a multithreaded client anyway.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on 0002, which is webOS specific]
---
--- a/src/wayland-client.c
+++ b/src/wayland-client.c
@@ -161,7 +161,7 @@ display_fatal_error(struct wl_display *display, int error)
 		wl_log("Exit client due to a fatal connection failure: %s\n",
 				strerror(error));
 		pthread_mutex_unlock(&display->mutex);
-		exit(1);
+		_exit(1);
 	}
 }
 
